<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johann Martin Honigberger</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Honigberger</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johann Martin Honigberger was a physician from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a> who served at the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahore">Lahore</a>. He later wrote a memoir, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-five-years-in-the-east">Thirty-five Years in the East</a>. His account is an important primary source on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johann-martin-honigberger.jpg" alt="Johann Martin Honigberger" width="318" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Honigberger.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
